  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/garra-culiciphaga-2/",
      "html": "<p>A quite new fish in the hobby is Garra culiciphaga. The small, peaceful and wonderful golden glossing cyprinid grows up to 8 cm long.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/garra-culiciphaga-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species is a Turkey endemic.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/garra-culiciphaga-2/",
      "html": "<p>The climatic conditions in its home country make Garra culiciphaga very tolerant against different temperatures. Most recent scientific research showed that this freshwater fish tolerates even strongly brackish water up to full salt concentration of the sea.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/garra-culiciphaga-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species was initially described by the French scientist Pellegrin in 1927 under the name Hemigrammocapoeta culiciphaga. It was placed in the genus Hemigrammocapoeta since 2015; recently specialized researchers see it rather in the genus Garra.</p>"
    }
  ],
